host1x-fence: add tegra194 to MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE

host1x-fence.ko only has tegra234-host1x in its MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE,
so udev never autoloads the module on tegra194 (Xavier). The driver
code already handles tegra194 via of_device_id in dev_file_open(),
but without the MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE entry the module is never loaded.

Add tegra194-host1x to the device table so udev triggers module
autoload on Xavier platforms, eliminating the "failed to open
host1x-fence device" warning from userspace.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>

--- a/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c
+++ b/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c
@@ -500,6 +500,7 @@
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id host1x_fence_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "nvidia,tegra194-host1x" },
 	{ .compatible = "nvidia,tegra234-host1x" },
 	{ },
 };
